## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a DP with partitioning and additive segment costs; uses prefix sums to optimize the transition to O(nk).

## Key Concepts

- DP on partitioning into k segments
- Prefix sums to compute segment costs in O(1)
- State transition optimization with a running max and backpointers
- Reconstruction of cut points

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxPartitionScore(A, k){
  const n = A.length;
  if (k <= 0 || k > n) return {score: 0, cuts: []};
  const diff = new Array(n-1).fill(0);
  for (let i = 0; i < n-1; i++) diff[i] = Math.abs(A[i+1] - A[i]);
  const pref = new Array(n).fill(0);
  for (let i = 1; i < n; i++) pref[i] = pref[i-1] + diff[i-1];
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => new Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const take = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => new Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) dp[i][1] = pref[i-1];
  for (let t = 2; t <= k; t++) {
    let best = -Infinity, bestP = -1;
    for (let i = t; i <= n; i++) {
      const p = i - 1;
      const val = dp[p][t-1] - pref[p];
      if (val > best) { best = val; bestP = p; }
      dp[i][t] = pref[i-1] + best;
      take[i][t] = bestP;
    }
  }
  let cuts = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (t > 0) {
    const p = take[i][t];
    cuts.push(i);
    i = p;
    t--;
  }
  cuts.reverse();
  return {score: dp[n][k], cuts};
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests concrete DP skills on string partitioning with reconstruction; approachable for beginners yet non-trivial.

## Key Concepts
- dp[i][t]: maximum sum for first i digits split into t parts
- val(j,i): integer value of s[j..i-1] (leading zeros allowed)
- transition: dp[i][t] = max_{j ∈ [t-1..i-1]} dp[j][t-1] + val(j,i)
- reconstruction: track prev to recover split indices
- complexity: O(n²k) time, O(nk) space; use BigInt for large results

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxSumSplit(s, k){
  const n = s.length;
  const val = (a,b)=> BigInt(s.slice(a,b));
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1n));
  const prev = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));

  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    dp[i][1] = val(0,i);
  }

  for(let t=2;t<=k;t++){
    for(let i=t;i<=n;i++){
      for(let j=t-1;j<i;j++){
        const candidate = dp[j][t-1] + val(j,i);
        if(candidate > dp[i][t]){
          dp[i][t] = candidate;
          prev[i][t] = j;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruct splits
  const splits = [];
  let curr = n, parts = k;
  while(parts > 1){
    const j = prev[curr][parts];
    splits.push(j);
    curr = j;
    parts--;
  }
  splits.reverse();

  return {maxSum: dp[n][k], splits};
}
```
